    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>OrderFort Fraud Shield helps WooCommerce stores reduce fake orders and suspicious checkout attempts with lightweight local protection that runs quietly in the background.</p>\n<p>Features include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Balanced local fraud scoring</li>\n<li>Checkout honeypot protection</li>\n<li>Disposable email detection</li>\n<li>Local review and block decisions</li>\n<li>Per-order risk metadata</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin zip in WordPress or install it manually.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin.</li>\n<li>Make sure WooCommerce is active.</li>\n<li>Open OrderFort Fraud Shield in the admin menu.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"does%20this%20plugin%20require%20woocommerce%3F\">\nDoes this plugin require WooCommerce?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. WooCommerce must be active.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"does%20the%20plugin%20read%20credit%20card%20numbers%3F\">\nDoes the plugin read credit card numbers?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. The plugin does not read or store raw payment card numbers or CVV/CVC values.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>3.2</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 7.0.2 and PHP 8.3.30.</li>\n<li>Added a Premium upgrade card with advanced settings and OLTORA shared cloud indicator benefits.</li>\n<li>Minor compatibility and bug-fix maintenance update.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>3.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Public release of OrderFort Fraud Shield.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Lightweight WooCommerce checkout protection with balanced local fraud scoring. Tested with WordPress 7.0.2 and PHP 8.3.30.",
